{
  "dom_id": "step-q84119",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Compute $\\text{E}[6X-4Z]$ if $\\text{E}[X]=2$ and $\\text{E}[Z]=2.$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[6X-4Z] & =6\\text{E}[X]-4\\text{E}[Z] \\\\  & =6(2)-4(2) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
